Practitioner and used intra-operatively during a Surgical Procedure.

16. Fulminant Hepatitis
A sub-massive to massive necrosis of the liver by the Hepatitis virus, leading precipitously to liver failure.
This diagnosis must be supported by all of the following:
I. Rapid decreasing of liver size;
II. Necrosis involving entire lobules, leaving only a collapsed reticular framework;
III. Rapid deterioration of liver function tests;
IV. Deepening jaundice; and
V. Hepatic encephalopathy.

The Benefit shall be payable upon satisfaction of all the following:
i. First Diagnosis of a covered cancer during the Policy Period;
ii. Diagnosis confirmed by histopathological evidence and certified by a Pathologist;
iii. Signs or symptoms first occurring after completion of the applicable Waiting Period.

The Sum Insured under this Benefit shall:
i. Be equal to the Base Policy Sum Insured;
ii. Be subject to a maximum cap of ₹50,00,000 per Insured Person;
iii. Be payable independent of and without reducing the Base Policy Sum Insured.

